# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vport-active-snapang-and-handle — SNAPANG does not reach the VPORT *Active record, which has no handle
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-vport-active-snapang
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

Found by the dxf-angles probe's clautolisp baseline run
(=scripts/run-dxf-angles-probe.sh --backend clautolisp=, 2026-10-23):

#+begin_example
(setvar "SNAPANG" (/ pi 9))
(getvar "SNAPANG")                         ; 0.349065850398866
(entget (tblobjname "VPORT" "*ACTIVE"))    ; ((-1 . <Entity name: TBL-...>)
                                           ;  (0 . "VPORT") (2 . "*Active"))
#+end_example

On AutoCAD / BricsCAD the VPORT *Active record carries the viewport
settings: 50 snap rotation angle (= SNAPANG, radians in entget), 51 view
twist, 10-17 corners / centre / snap / grid, 40-42 height, aspect, lens,
70-79 modes, and a 5 handle. clautolisp's seeded record has only 0 and 2,
so tblsearch / tblobjname + entget show none of it, and the DXF writer
emits a VPORT record without handle or 50.

* Proposal

Mirror the viewport sysvars (SNAPANG, SNAPBASE, SNAPUNIT, GRIDUNIT,
SNAPMODE, GRIDMODE, VIEWCTR, VIEWSIZE, VIEWTWIST via 51 ...) into the
*Active record (or compute it on read), give the seeded symbol-table
records handles, and compare with the dxf-angles probe's vendor reports
(=DXFANG ENTGET vport 50/51=, =DXFANG FILE vport 50/51=).


Resolved (2026-10-25, clautolisp 2.3.65)
----------------------------------------

The handle was there already (the seeded records get one since
ENSURE-RECORD-HANDLE: the 2026-10-25 baseline shows "HANDLE vport VPORT
18"). The groups were not. The vendors' dxf-angles reports and DXF, read
again:

| after (setvar "SNAPANG" (/ pi 9)) | entget *Active 50 | its DXF 50 |
|-----------------------------------+-------------------+------------|
| BricsCAD V25 / V26                | 0.349066          | 20.0       |
| AutoCAD 2022                      | 0                 | 20.0       |

BricsCAD updates the record at once; AutoCAD keeps it as stored until it
saves. Now (cador/source/viewports.lisp, *RECORD-LAYOUTS* in entity-api):
- the *Active entget shows the vendors' groups in their order (2 70 10 11
  12-17 40 42-44 50 51 71-78); a group mirrors its viewport sysvar
  (*VPORT-SYSVARS*: VIEWCTR 12, SNAPBASE 13, SNAPUNIT 14, GRIDUNIT 15,
  VIEWDIR 16, TARGET 17, VIEWSIZE 40, LENSLENGTH 42, FRONTZ 43, BACKZ 44,
  SNAPANG 50, VIEWTWIST 51, VIEWMODE 71, UCSICON 74, SNAPMODE 75, GRIDMODE
  76, SNAPSTYL 77, SNAPISOPAIR 78); 72 (circle zoom) 1000 on AutoCAD, 100
  on BricsCAD, as their DXF have it;
- a setvar of one stores the new value in the record under the BricsCAD
  dialects, the old one (if none stored yet) under the others;
- a save (CADOR-SAVE-DRAWING) stores every current value, in that order,
  so the DXF's *Active has 50 20.0 as both CADs write it.
Test VPORT-ACTIVE-SHOWS-THE-VIEWPORT-SYSVARS-AS-EACH-PRODUCT-DOES.

Not modelled: 41 (the display's aspect), 65 and the UCS groups 110-146,
348 / 60 / 61 / 292 / 282 / 141 / 142 / 63 / 421; a DXF read does not set
the sysvars from its *Active record; tiled viewports beyond the first
have no *Active record of their own; TBLSEARCH still shows the stored
record only.
